senses.gloss:
(II)--the consort of काम. Hearing that he was burnt by शिव, she clad herself in sorrowful clothes. श्या- मला restored him back to life, and in her presence both were married again;
1: Br. IV. ३०. ३७-51; M. 7. १३; १००. ३२; १५४. २१९, २७२-3;
a शक्ति;
2: Br. IV. १९. ६४-71; ४४; ७२.
mother of हर्ष;
3: वा. १०. ३८.
प्रीति became her co-wife; after the burning of काम, was माया- वती in शम्बर's house and brought up Pradyumna (an incarnation of काम);
4: Vi. I. 7. ३१; V. २७. ३०.
Image of, with swan.
5: M. २६१. ५५.

(IV)--when the Asuras were born to प्रजापति night came into being; ety.; three यामस् of the night are full of darkness--त्रियामिका; then प्रजापति took another guise and created the devas; आसुरि of tamas quality;
1: वा. 9. 6-१५; Br. II. १३. १४.
no [page३-071+ ३०] night for the region to the north of Meru and south of लोका- loka as the sun is far removed and the earth is surrounded by the lekha;
2: वा. ५०. १०८.
for the पितृस् is सुक्लपक्ष;
3: Ib. ५१. ११; ५७. 9.
enters water in the morning.
4: Ib. ५३. १४.
